10. Menu Option 1 — Register New Customer
Ask the employee for the customer's full name, national ID, optional phone number, and tier.
Before creating the customer, validate the information. The name cannot be empty. The national ID must not already
belong to another customer. If a phone number is entered, it must contain only digits and must be between 7 and 15
digits.
When registration succeeds, generate a customer ID automatically and display the new customer's ID and details.
Example: if the generated ID is 1001, the program may display: Customer registered successfully.
Customer ID: 1001.
11. Menu Option 2 — Open New Account
Ask for the customer ID. If it does not exist, do not create an account.
Then ask the employee to select an account type and enter the required information for that type. Check the minimum
opening balance configured for the selected type. If the amount is invalid, the account must not be created.
The system generates the account number automatically, creates the account record, associates it with the customer,
stores it in the account storage, and updates the customer's account count.

