12. Menu Option 3 — Deposit Money
Ask for an account number and a deposit amount.
Find the account. The account must exist and must allow transactions. The amount must be positive and should satisfy
the minimum transaction amount chosen for the system.
If successful, increase the account balance, increase its successful transaction count, and display the new balance.
Example: Current balance = $500. Deposit = $200. New balance = $700.
13. Menu Option 4 — Withdraw Money
Ask for an account number and withdrawal amount. Find the account and validate its status and the amount.
The withdrawal must then follow the rules of the particular account type:
• Savings: reject the operation if the resulting balance would be below zero; on success, increase the monthly
withdrawal counter.
• Current: allow the balance to become negative, but never below the allowed overdraft limit.
• Fixed Deposit: reject the operation if the account has not matured. If it has matured, allow the withdrawal according
to the account rules.
Every successful withdrawal increases the transaction count. Every rejected withdrawal must leave the balance
unchanged.
14. Menu Option 5 — Transfer Between Accounts
Ask for a source account number, destination account number, and amount.
Both accounts must exist and must be different. The source must be able to complete the withdrawal. The destination
must be able to receive the deposit.
A transfer is one complete operation. If the source withdrawal succeeds but the destination deposit cannot be
completed, the money must be restored to the source so that the failed transfer does not lose funds.
Example: Source has $1,000. Transfer $250. If successful, source becomes $750 and destination
increases by $250.
Display a clear success or failure message.

