15. Menu Option 6 — Display Customer Accounts
Ask for a customer ID. If the customer exists, display the customer's information and all accounts belonging to that
customer.
For each account, display at least:
• Account number
• Account type
• Balance
• Status
• Transaction count
At the end, display the combined balance of all accounts owned by that customer.
16. Menu Option 7 — Display All Branch Accounts
Display all accounts currently stored by the branch. A useful display should include account number, owner name,
type, balance, status, and transaction count.
If there are no accounts, display a suitable message instead of showing an empty or confusing table.
17. Menu Option 8 — Search Account by Number
Ask for an account number and search the stored accounts.
The search should be case-insensitive if your account-number format contains letters. If found, display the complete
information relevant to that account, including information specific to its type.
For example, a current account can display its overdraft limit, while a fixed deposit can display its duration, elapsed
months, and whether it has matured.
18. Menu Option 9 — Search Accounts by Type
Ask the employee to choose an account type. Display all accounts of that type.
At the end, display the number of matching accounts and the combined balance of those accounts.

