19. Menu Option 10 — Close an Account
An account cannot be closed simply because the employee selects the close option.
Before closing, verify that:
• The account exists.
• The account is not already closed.
• The balance is exactly $0.
• A fixed deposit is not still locked before maturity.
If all conditions are satisfied, mark the account as closed and update the customer's number of open accounts.
20. Menu Option 0 — Exit
The program should stop its menu loop and display a short farewell message.
21. Input Validation
The application should handle invalid input without crashing. At minimum, consider the following situations:
• Selecting a menu number that does not exist.
• Entering text where a number is expected.
• Entering a negative amount or zero when a positive amount is required.
• Using an account number that does not exist.
• Using a customer ID that does not exist.
• Registering a duplicate national ID.
• Trying to transact on a frozen or closed account.
• Trying to withdraw more than the allowed amount.
• Trying to close an account with a non-zero balance.
• Trying to withdraw from an unmatured fixed deposit.

